# Yasvik storefront type & layout

Shop and Product Detail are the **canonical** customer UI. Home, About, Our Roots, Contact, Stories, Checkout, and combos must match them — do not invent a second type system per page.

## Fonts (only these two)

| Role | Face | Tailwind |
|------|------|----------|
| Titles / display | **Cormorant Garamond** | `font-cormorant` |
| Body / UI / buttons / labels | **DM Sans** | `font-inter` (legacy class name; face is DM Sans) |

- Do **not** use Syne, Inter, Playfair, Roboto, or bare `system-ui` for storefront UI.
- `font-syne` is aliased to Cormorant for safety — prefer rewriting to `font-cormorant`.
- Title weight: **`font-semibold` (600)**. Avoid `font-light` / `font-thin` on headings.
- Body: `font-inter` with `text-sm` / `text-base` and muted ink `text-deep-forest/70`.

## Ink & surfaces

Prefer theme tokens, not one-off hex:

- Page: `bg-warm-cream` / `text-deep-forest`
- Cards: `bg-white` + `border-soft-border`
- Labels: `retailClasses.label` (uppercase, tracked, `font-inter`)

`text-rain-cloud` equals deep forest — prefer **`text-deep-forest`** on new work.

## Layout alignment

Use shared bundles from `@/brand/retailTheme`:

```js
import { retailClasses } from '@/brand/retailTheme';

// page shell
retailClasses.page
retailClasses.container        // max-w-[1400px] px-4 md:px-8  — same as Shop/PDP
retailClasses.containerNarrow  // long-form (About)
retailClasses.titlePage | titleLg | titleMd
retailClasses.body | bodyLg
retailClasses.btnPrimary | btnOutline
```

- Do not invent a different max-width or horizontal padding per marketing page.
- Section rhythm: one purpose, one heading (`titleLg` / `titleMd`), short supporting `body` line.

## When building UI

1. Start from `retailClasses` / existing Shop or PDP patterns.
2. If a new heading style is needed, add it to `retailTheme.js` — do not hard-code a third font.
3. Admin (`/admin`) may keep denser Inter/admin patterns; this rule is for **customer-facing** surfaces.
